{"skill":{"slug":"ralph-loops","displayName":"Ralph Loops"},"version":{"version":"1.0.2","createdAt":1769936024664,"changelog":"Added warning: don't block conversation while monitoring loops","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SETUP.md","size":1985,"sha256":"073c1f84d0e478133a25833f00230477cf27962eafae696f8f93dc2f7a2aa523","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":20844,"sha256":"c3124afa41813ae2b9462c5812349a52d513be1bdb39d7bb0eec36070a70f59f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"dashboard/lib/cost-calculator.mjs","size":1364,"sha256":"562c3c15e6e3fc887081781df32d0d87e95688abeed5d2a3effd752dde4fec19","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"dashboard/lib/loop-detector.mjs","size":9716,"sha256":"31ccdc65740ab0457d9d50f23da0bbcd116144fd031c6154f296cee994fea9a7","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"dashboard/lib/ralph-reader.mjs","size":8582,"sha256":"9e1dd5ec4cde9b3896d86fcdd63333a0546e0eb69ae5ee2a31b41b687f4f1d75","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"dashboard/lib/transcript-reader.mjs","size":5802,"sha256":"f270fb7d8ee4fc7b521227a17d582d59fc99f715e81396a0b45828817c20f030","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"dashboard/package-lock.json","size":30276,"sha256":"8e83f3880be64487e2fe6bcaacf2a4237341bf30eb2b4c3692602c8d6273ab0f","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"dashboard/package.json","size":393,"sha256":"d5c46f4ea8a83ffdb22cf789906ab34abc46db5ca19522188f29f6df032842fe","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"dashboard/public/dashboard.js","size":15597,"sha256":"ad98aee33309805fe2434258a35ab362c2bdafa81db23af61336bd5a1d46eb23","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"dashboard/public/index.html","size":14041,"sha256":"04a921bff454a3330f7557103c92a30fcda679f8fd52ed3aa8bc0bbb2d5fe424","contentType":"text/html"},{"path":"dashboard/public/style.css","size":7566,"sha256":"799015bc9549f1b7370e905b28770463ec016ecda013b415b120586e7b7f0754","contentType":"text/css"},{"path":"dashboard/routes/loops.mjs","size":3881,"sha256":"fe9badf0ee1579d0a3b175e47f4a4a1083be3a9113525399026e2514e2983637","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"dashboard/server.mjs","size":2454,"sha256":"e03d8d661370b226651883d44643f25b1121f6e3183a4e5e518a3663162fe4a4","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"dashboard/start.sh","size":406,"sha256":"8a89547d7213664c428ed39d7c416b1c7cb8d91ee36abcb436c18ba2993812b7","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/ralph-loop.mjs","size":16832,"sha256":"b1bf5f641f484a548b96a42d73a0f2541ab2b0883ea5c0492a115bfea9a0b0fe","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"templates/AGENTS.md","size":626,"sha256":"a1cbd0ad0be21ac91721badac871480146a263eeb6fafe637d3e87e457683f78","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"templates/PROMPT_build.md","size":3717,"sha256":"0df0f4f7cf04f798c5a8b8ba859b64dd7cbed3f965504de6c198ef82da719174","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"templates/PROMPT_plan.md","size":2009,"sha256":"0ef566a1c139e5dbb175127d1e6004c68864676b7474271331577ef5bd224361","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"templates/loop.sh","size":3495,"sha256":"df502866a9f58a885042d6c5e6e406c69fa8a4cbe82c02f69245ded580bd546a","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"templates/requirements-interview.md","size":6467,"sha256":"6ae8482fbccc6c26860c67ddd5f1f8b17c0cbd86cc512a9fc56b8a5538aefe7a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2358,"sha256":"2371cf13f403b76804a757268cae5bb67d98be16094d1fd86417c60791577749","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789026505516,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"46557e810873f3bed70544b354c1a724a8db03804a8450a9eec622fa5d48b5eb","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/46557e810873f3bed70544b354c1a724a8db03804a8450a9eec622fa5d48b5eb","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: ralph-loops\nVersion: 1.0.2\n\nThis skill is classified as suspicious due to its reliance on `--dangerously-skip-permissions` for the Claude CLI, which grants the AI agent full system access, bypassing all built-in safeguards. Additionally, the `scripts/ralph-loop.mjs` script includes a `checkCmd` argument that allows arbitrary command execution via `execSync`, creating a direct command injection vector if the agent's arguments can be manipulated. The skill also instructs the agent to perform `git push` operations and use the `browser` tool to open URLs (e.g., `browser action=open targetUrl=\"http://localhost:PORT\"`), which are powerful capabilities that, while intended for development, significantly increase the attack surface for prompt injection or misuse. These risky capabilities are present in `SKILL.md`, `scripts/ralph-loop.mjs`, `templates/loop.sh`, and `templates/PROMPT_build.md`.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160642724},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":38,"checkedAt":1789026505516},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed autonomous development loop, but its defaults run agents with permission checks disabled and expose underprotected dashboard, process, and Git controls.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The documentation recommends Docker or VM isolation, reduced credentials, and restricted network access, but the implementation does not enforce those boundaries. The runner uses ~/clawd as its working directory, state is stored in /tmp, and the dashboard enables permissive CORS without authentication.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation uses ordinary npm dependencies for the dashboard and documented Claude Code setup. The lockfile includes path-to-regexp 0.1.12 via Express, which is a dependency risk for an HTTP dashboard but not evidence of malicious packaging.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill discloses that autonomous mode bypasses permissions, but the default examples and templates do not require a scoped project directory, review gate, or explicit approval before high-impact actions such as remote pushes, tags, and dashboard kill operations.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill writes state and done markers in /tmp, archives histories under ~/clawd/logs/ralph-archive, reads local Clawdbot transcript files, exposes process termination, and mutates Git state. These behaviors fit the purpose but carry high impact without strong containment.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The purpose is coherent: iterative autonomous development with a monitoring dashboard. However, the shipped runner and templates intentionally launch Claude with permission checks bypassed, can edit the workspace, and can automatically commit, push, and tag repository changes.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable running an autonomous coding loop with broad local authority. Use a disposable branch or isolated VM/container, provide only task-specific credentials, disable or restrict the dashboard to loopback with authentication, review diffs before any push or tag, and do not run it in repositories or workspaces containing sensitive files until the dashboard command-injection/XSS and unauthenticated control issues are fixed.","findings":"[AE1] unexpected: Downgraded: the referenced ralph-loop.mjs file is present in the artifact and was inspected locally, so the partial-inspection concern is not supported after review.\n[SQP-2] expected: Confirmed: --dangerously-skip-permissions is central to the autonomous loop and is disclosed, but using it by default with broad workspace access and no enforced sandbox is a material Review concern.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Confirmed in PROMPT_build.md and loop.sh: automatic git push and tagging go beyond local iterative implementation and lack an explicit human review gate.\n[T05] unexpected: Confirmed: the dashboard exposes process-control APIs without authentication or origin restrictions, and the agent runner operates with broad permissions across ~/clawd.\n[T09] unexpected: Confirmed: dashboard killLoop interpolates state-derived values into shell commands, and index.html renders loop-state fields through innerHTML, creating command-injection and stored-XSS risks if local state is attacker-controlled.\n[SC4] unexpected: Confirmed: package-lock.json includes path-to-regexp 0.1.12. This is a dependency vulnerability concern, not purpose-aligned behavior or malicious intent.\n[P6] expected: Downgraded: the cited code returns the user-supplied prompt text or prompt file contents for the loop; it does not independently expose system prompts.\n[MP3] expected: Downgraded: the cited state mutations are loop bookkeeping in the local state file, not persistent agent memory poisoning.\n[E1] expected: Downgraded: the Anthropic API curl example is a documented alternative interface for running Claude with a user-provided API key, not hidden exfiltration in the runtime path.\n[TM1] expected: Downgraded: git reset --hard appears as a manual escape-hatch suggestion, not an automatic destructive action, though users should treat it carefully.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789026505516}}}}}